>> title: Egg Foo Young
>> category: Stir-Fries
>> tags: eggs, pork, bean sprouts, chinese, skillet
>> counters: Takeout Counter, One Pot
>> aka: egg foo young, egg fu yung, egg foo yong, roast pork egg foo young, 芙蓉蛋, fu rong dan
>> pairs-with: house-brown-sauce
>> servings: 4
>> time: 25 min
>> washing-up: the skillet, a bowl to beat the eggs and fold the filling in
>> keeps: not at all — the patty is fried and the sauce has it soggy in minutes; both are five-minute jobs

>> step: beat well, until it is one colour
Beat @eggs{6%large} with @light soy sauce{1%tsp}, @white pepper{1/4%tsp}, and @kosher salt{1/4%tsp} until the yolks and whites are one colour — this is an omelette patty, not a scramble, so it wants beating properly.

>> step: fold the filling through
Fold @bean sprouts{1%cup}(90 g), @napa cabbage{1%cup}(75 g; finely shredded), @scallions{3}(thinly sliced), and @char siu{4%oz}(115 g; diced) into @&(~1)beaten eggs{}.

>> step: fry 3 min a side, four patties
Fry @&(~1)mixture{} in @peanut oil{1/4%cup}(60 mL) in a hot #skillet{} as four patties, a ladleful at a time, ~fry{3%min} a side, spooning oil over the top so the middle sets while the edges go lacy.

>> step: ladle the gravy over
Ladle @house brown sauce{1%cup}(240 mL; hot) over @&(~1)patties{} at the table.
